From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:48:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] VICTORY_PIPELINE_X_DUMP=<folder>: what device methods
 0x1c8 and 0x218 are handed

Off when unset; the two methods fail as they did (E_NOTIMPL) either way.
A run's log counted 16,384 calls of 0x1c8 and 2,048 of 0x218: pipelines
the title goes without. Their descriptions are not the PC ones: 0x1c8
names a root signature and six pieces (address, length), 0x218 thirteen
words with four such pieces, two addresses and a hash-like word. To
write the methods, the pieces themselves have to be read.

With the switch, the first 8 calls of each method write to the folder:
- x<slot>-<call>.txt: the description's first 64 words and its pieces,
- x<slot>-<call>-w<word>-<bytes>.bin: each piece (an address followed by
  a length of up to 1 MiB; an address alone: 256 bytes), read through
  the kernel, so a piece that is not mapped is said and skipped.
The files hold the title's data and stay on this machine.

Tests: the pieces of the two descriptions a run logged
(the_pieces_of_a_0x1c8_..., the_pieces_of_a_0x218_...). victory-gpu:
156 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
